 "confidence": "medium",
 "notes_for_editor": "NRHP nomination (05000743) is not digitised, so the 2005 listing is left out of the prose (only the record and Wikipedia state it). Bulletin 1928 is badly OCR'd; printed pages 229-230 are inferred from the OCR and the 1924-29 index, please check against the scan. Light Board volume pages not determined. 2018 buyer unknown; LighthouseFriends still says Coast Guard owns it, and the NHLPA table lists it oddly beside 'Maryland' in one column (column OCR). Optics conflict: LF/Lake Carriers 4th order, USLHS original 3rd order; focal height 70 ft (Bulletin) vs 65 ft (USLHS). Crittenden's earlier stations come from LighthouseFriends only. Jarvis 'at least 1959' per USLHS roster. Muskegon grounding 1908 only from LighthouseFriends. Fact-check 2026-10-27: Lighthouse Service Bulletin also calls the lantern fourth-order (only USLHS says third order original); LighthouseFriends says work wrapped up July 1927 vs Bulletin August 1927 (both stated). George R. McRae appears only in USLHS. USCG crew from the USLHS roster added to the keeper list. Bulletin pages 229-230 consistent with the 1924-29 index entry ('in commission 229-230'). Light-House Board request was already a repeat by the 1896 report, so no 'first' request is claimed.",
